On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:51:51 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Update lab-claude jail.conf to mount /jails/data/lab-claude/dot-claude/
> to ~claude/.claude/.

Done in patch 1 of "[PATCH 0/2] jails: Persist lab-claude's Claude
state" [1]. It is a nullfs rw mount, and exec.prepare creates the mount
point. The README now lists the host dir, which must be owned by
15000:15000. I could not build or start a jail from in here, so this
is untested. The one thing I would check is that /home/claude ends up
owned by claude after a fresh build, because exec.prepare creates it
before pw useradd -m runs.

> However I think it would be more useful if we could store
> the config in a dir and just mount that, and set the config file with an
> env var.
>
> Research the .claude.json file, see if it can be moved elsewhere, and if
> there are any issues with including it in .claude/ itself.

Yes, it can be moved. I read the Claude Code 2.1.283 installed in the
jail. When CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is set, the global config is
$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/.claude.json. Settings, credentials, history,
projects, and plugins move to $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR as well. Patch 2 sets
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/claude/.claude in the claude user's
.login_conf, so .claude.json moves into the mounted dir and nothing
else changes location. No second mount is needed.

I found no issues with keeping it inside .claude/. Claude already
writes its .claude.json backups to ~/.claude/backups, and the
device-keys file is always under ~/.claude. There is also a legacy
fallback that works without the env var: ~/.claude/.config.json is
preferred over ~/.claude.json. I used the documented variable instead.

The existing ~claude/.claude.json is not migrated. To keep the current
state, copy ~claude/.claude/ into /jails/data/lab-claude/dot-claude and
~claude/.claude.json to dot-claude/.claude.json before restarting the
jail.

